  "description": "KENDAL PLACE",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal constitutes development under the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, and the local planning authority is not satisfied that, based on the drawings submitted as part of the application, this proposal falls within any class of 'permitted development' specified within Schedule 2 to the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\nINFORMATIVE: The proposed development fails to comply with Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) as Condition 6 of planning permission ref.86/W/3807 removes permitted development rights for extensions, additions or enlargements at the subject property and therefore the proposed replacement dormer and conservatory works cannot be carried out under the GPDO. The works would therefore require planning permission.\r\n\r\n"
